# String localization

User-facing copy lives in Android resources. Default English is
`app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml`.

Locales currently in this project:

- `values/` — default (English)
- `values-sr/` — Serbian (Latin)

## When adding or changing a string

1. Put the key in `values/strings.xml`.
2. Add the **same key** to every other `app/src/main/res/values-*/strings.xml`.
3. Translate the value. Keep format placeholders (`%1$d`, `%s`) and argument order.
4. Keep the same XML comment groups as the default file.
5. Do not leave a new key in English-only; Android would fall back for other locales.

```xml
<!-- values/strings.xml -->
<string name="library_empty">No exercises yet</string>

<!-- values-sr/strings.xml -->
<string name="library_empty">Još nema vežbi</string>
```

Brand names such as `app_name` may stay unchanged in every locale.

If you add a new `values-<locale>/` folder, copy every key from `values/strings.xml`
and translate that full file. Preview-only literals in `@Preview` functions stay
on `stringResource` keys, not hardcoded text.
